Argus
=====

Argus is based on ScamGuard (https://github.com/abgolor/ScamGuard)
Copyright (c) 2026 Abraham Golor (github.com/abgolor)

The ScamGuard repository does not carry an open-source licence. Its code is
used, renamed and modified in Argus with the permission of its author. That
permission was given to the Argus owner; it is not an open-source licence and
does not extend to third parties. Changes in Argus: the product was renamed
from ScamGuard to Argus, the Nigerian Pidgin translation was replaced with
Hindi, and the app was rewritten in Flutter (the scam rules are a Dart port of
the original Kotlin engine).


Third-party material included in Argus:

1. Gemma (the on-device model shipped in the standard and lite APKs)
   The full Gemma notice, use restrictions, Terms of Use and Prohibited Use Policy
   are at the end of this file, and in the app under About.


2. Atkinson Hyperlegible Next (app font: app/src/main/res/font/atkinson_hyperlegible_next_*.ttf)
   Static weights (400, 600, 700) were
   instanced from the variable font in github.com/google/fonts (ofl/atkinsonhyperlegiblenext)
